    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Overview</strong>:<br>This is a sci-fi space strategy puzzle-solving, <strong>level-based</strong> combat game with an innovative combat system. Players can craft battle strategies, assign specific ships, and customize ship modules. The game features multiple-ending storylines and freely selectable side quests. After completing the main campaign, endless combat mode unlocks, where unique AI enemies dynamically adapt their tactics based on battle conditions.</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Features</strong>:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Unique Combat System</strong>: Adopts a &quot;hands-off&quot; design\u2014far from dull! Players must pre-plan deployments and outthink enemies using skills and commands rather than relying solely on ship stats or gear. During battles, observe ship behavior and adjust tactics in real-time. Main missions provide one-time-only intelligence, while side quests offer hints or let players investigate independently (note: repairing the flagship in the first position costs a side quest attempt).</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Strategic Depth</strong>: Like card games, players anticipate enemy strategies (e.g., pirate generals have fixed loadouts) and design tactics based on objectives\u2014lure the enemy deeper, prioritize eliminating leaders, focus fire, etc.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Notes</strong>:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Early-Game Pacing</strong>: The prologue may feel slow due to tutorials (e.g., installing weapons, selecting armor, building tank ships, skill/command effects, terrain impacts). However, side quests offer deeper tutorials, and the experience improves significantly later with richer mechanics and maxed-out fleet sizes.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Command Overlap Risks</strong>: Overlapping movement orders and skill triggers may cause unintended outcomes (e.g., ordering a ship to advance for 60 seconds while simultaneously retreating within the same timeframe leads to undefined behavior).</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Formation Strategy</strong>: Formations work best for fast ships; slow vessels risk being destroyed before deploying. Choose wisely!</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Future Updates</strong>:<br>Updates/DLCs will depend on community reception. Planned content includes:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Level System</strong>: Expand with more stages. [V1.073 complete].</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Character System</strong>: Add character profiles with art, lore, and unique abilities [V1.07 complete].</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Weapon System</strong>: Introduce new gear and equipment.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Ship System</strong>: Add more playable vessels.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Long-Term Vision</strong>:<br>5. <strong>City System</strong>: Requires significant development time/resources.<br>6. <strong>Sovereignty System</strong><br>7. <strong>Economy/Trade System</strong><br>8. <strong>Miscellaneous</strong>: Randomized items, blueprint crafting, ship production, alien ecosystems, and more.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p>",
